---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="VMTR-01 Privacy Policy — Vireal" description="Privacy Policy for the VMTR-01 Android multichannel USB audio recorder.">
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow"><a href="/vmtr01/">VMTR-01</a> / Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated: October 18, 2026</p>

    <p>
      VMTR-01 is an Android app developed by Vireal for recording audio from compatible USB audio devices.
      This policy explains how the app handles recordings, analytics, and diagnostics.
    </p>

    <h2>Audio recordings</h2>
    <p>
      Recordings are stored on your Android device, including in shared device storage when you save or
      publish them. VMTR-01 does not upload the contents of your audio recordings to Vireal or to analytics
      and diagnostics providers. You control access to recordings you export or share from your device.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      VMTR-01 uses Amplitude Analytics to understand app usage, USB audio compatibility, and reliability.
      Depending on the app build and actions taken, analytics data may include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>app version, Android version, device manufacturer and model;</li>
      <li>USB audio device characteristics and audio settings, such as channel count and sample rate;</li>
      <li>feature use, recording duration, and success or failure events;</li>
      <li>pseudonymous device or installation identifiers and technical SDK metadata.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Crash and error diagnostics</h2>
    <p>
      VMTR-01 uses Sentry to investigate crashes and application errors. Diagnostic events may include
      exception information and stack traces, operation or error categories, and app, OS, and device
      details. Network infrastructure used by these services may also process IP addresses as part of
      providing their services. The app is designed to minimize personal information in diagnostic events.
    </p>

    <h2>Information not intentionally collected</h2>
    <p>
      VMTR-01 is not designed to send audio contents, recording filenames, user-created recording
      metadata, account names, email addresses, or precise location to Amplitude or Sentry.
      VMTR-01 does not require an account to record audio.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Technical data may be processed by <a href="https://amplitude.com/privacy">Amplitude</a> and
      <a href="https://sentry.io/privacy/">Sentry</a> under their respective privacy practices.
      Processing and retention periods for service data are subject to their applicable settings
      and policies. Some processing may take place outside your country of residence.
    </p>

    <h2>Data controls</h2>
    <p>
      You can remove recordings from your device using VMTR-01 or your device's file management tools.
      Clearing app data or uninstalling the app may remove locally stored settings, but recordings
      exported to shared storage may remain until you delete them. For questions about analytics or
      diagnostic data, contact the developer using the link below.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy as the app evolves. The updated date at the top indicates the latest
      published version.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For questions or privacy requests, contact Vireal through
      <a href="https://github.com/vireal01">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/vmtr01/">← Back to VMTR-01</a></p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
